WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.040
Привет, Фрэнс!

00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.400
Welcome to привет, русский, эпизод 20,

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.100
for 20th of May 2020.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.200
I'm Olya,

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:10.000
and we've got some great Russian words to learn today.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:11.540
Поехали, let's go.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.040
Let's start with our word of the day.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:16.200
The Russian word is хлеб.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:17.020
хлеб.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:18.380
That means bread.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.700
Say it was me slowly, хлеб.

00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:22.580
Now again, at normal speed.

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:23.380
хлеб.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:25.480
It sounds a little like club,

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:29.280
but this word is the stuff of life on every Russian table.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.080
Try this simple sentence with me.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:33.020
Я М хлеб.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.800
That means I eat bread.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:36.020
Repeat after me.

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:37.320
Я М хлеб.

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.160
Great job!

00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.820
Now we will build more words around food.

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:43.580
The next word is молоко, молоко.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:44.600
That means milk.

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:46.700
Repeat after me, молоко.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.280
Imagine a cow saying move while giving you milk.

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.920
That memory hook helps you remember it.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:54.600
Let's add another word.

00:00:55.160 --> 00:00:56.680
The Russian word is яйцо.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:57.600
Яйцо.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:58.940
That means egg.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:01.100
Repeat after me, яйцо.

00:01:01.680 --> 00:01:03.940
Say yay when you find an egg for breakfast.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:05.720
Now say it in a sentence.

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:07.180
Это яйцо.

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:09.120
That means this is an egg.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.580
Repeat after me, это яйцо.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:12.900
Let's keep going.

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:14.840
The next word is сыр.

00:01:15.160 --> 00:01:15.420
сыр.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:16.680
That means cheese.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:17.960
Repeat after me.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:18.620
сыр.

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.060
It sounds like sir.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.060
A fancy sir who loves cheese.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:23.680
Try this sentence.

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:25.080
сыр вкусный.

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.060
That means that cheese is delicious.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:29.080
We have two more food words.

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:31.040
The Russian word is frooked.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:31.700
Frooked.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:33.080
That means fruit.

00:01:33.480 --> 00:01:34.240
Repeat after me.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:35.000
Frooked.

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.160
It is almost exactly like the English word fruit.

00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:41.000
The last food word is овощ.

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:41.860
овощ.

00:01:42.080 --> 00:01:42.940
That means vegetable.

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:44.180
Repeat after me.

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:44.960
овощ.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.200
Think of all fresh vegetables from the garden.

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.880
Now let's learn one more useful word.

00:01:51.360 --> 00:01:53.080
The Russian word is вкусный.

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:53.820
вкусный.

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:55.240
That means delicious.

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:56.320
Repeat after me.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:57.060
вкусный.

00:01:57.360 --> 00:01:58.700
вкус is like taste.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:01:59.980
Вот о яйме Ending.

00:02:00.280 --> 00:02:01.240
Here is a sentence.

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:02.480
хлеб вкусный.

00:02:02.960 --> 00:02:04.380
That means the bread is delicious.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:05.460
Repeat after me.

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:06.760
хлеб вкусный.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:08.180
You are doing so well.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.300
Now we move to our grammar byte.

00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.240
Russian nouns change their ending

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.240
depending on whether they are the subject

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:15.820
or the object in a sentence.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.460
For example, хлеб becomes хлеба.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:19.880
When you say you eat bread.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:21.440
Я и м хлеба.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:25.100
English usually shows meaning that word order instead of endings.

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:28.260
Russian endings lead sentences stay flexible

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.840
while keeping the same idea.

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:33.260
Now you can say more natural phrases like this one.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:35.260
Here is our culture corner.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:37.680
In Russia, bread is more than food.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.300
It is a symbol of hospitality and respect.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:43.340
Guests are often welcomed with bread and salt

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.020
on a special embroidered cloth.

00:02:45.580 --> 00:02:47.920
This tradition shows how sharing simple foods

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:49.020
brings people together.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:51.040
Now for practice time.

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:54.340
For kids, draw your favorite food from today's list

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:56.120
and label it with a Russian word.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:02:58.600
Then tell a grown-up what it is in Russian.

00:02:59.140 --> 00:03:00.900
For adults, next time you shop,

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.460
practice saying the Russian names for bread, milk and cheese.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:06.420
Out loud in the grocery aisle.

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:09.020
Want to know a secret about one of today's words?

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:10.660
The Russian word magazine

00:03:10.660 --> 00:03:14.140
and the English word magazine are actually the same word.

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.680
They both come from the Arabic magazine,

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.780
meaning a storehouse or treasury.

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:22.480
This word traveled through Persian and Turkish trade routes

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.180
and arrived in Russian in the 17th century

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:26.840
as a place to keep goods.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.840
But be careful, the Russian word magazine sounds like magazine

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:32.220
but actually means shop.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:36.900
Next time you see a magazine, remember it is cousins with magazine.

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:40.360
They both come from the same root for storing things.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:42.820
That connection is your secret shortcut

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:44.080
to remembering it forever.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.600
Молодец, that means well done.

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.620
Remember, every expert started as a beginner.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:53.060
Practice saying today's words out loud even just once

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.440
and you'll be amazed how fast you learn.

00:03:55.880 --> 00:03:58.920
See you next time, poka, that's Russian for buy.

